INT. HOLLOWAY FUNERAL HOME - RECEPTION ROOM - DAY

Folding tables. Casserole dishes. Black dresses. A waiter circles with a tray of deviled eggs.

Nora Vance, 50s, widow, stiff smile, stands by the coffee urn. Her late husband's brother, Vic, 60s, hovers too close.

VIC
Nora. We need to talk about the will.

NORA
Not today, Vic.

VIC
It's today or it's a lawyer.

Two TEENAGERS by the buffet snicker at their phones. A beagle noses under a table, steals an egg.

Nora's phone RINGS. She checks it. UNKNOWN NUMBER. She answers.

MAN (V.O.)
(distorted, over phone)
Don't let Vic near the study.

Nora's eyes snap to Vic. He is already walking toward the hallway.

NORA
(low)
Vic!

THE MOURNERS turn as one. The beagle barks. Vic breaks into a run.

SMASH CUT TO:

INT. HOLLOWAY FUNERAL HOME - HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS

A door slams.
